---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Terms of Use | Piano Chord Explorer" description="Practical terms for using free Piano Chord Explorer music lessons, interactive piano tools, original diagrams and local recordings." canonicalPath="/terms/" noindex={true} crumbs={[{name:'Terms',href:'/terms/'}]}>
 <section class="container page-hero">
  <span class="eyebrow">SITE TERMS</span><h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="lead">Effective November 15, 2026. These terms describe how visitors may use the free educational materials and browser tools offered by Piano Chord Explorer.</p>
 </section>
 <section class="container section-compact">
  <article class="panel prose narrow" style="margin:auto">
   <h2>Free educational tools</h2>
   <p>The site provides music-theory explanations, chord diagrams, practice tools, downloadable reference sheets and browser-synthesized piano audio for learning. No account or subscription is required for the current features. Explanations and generated chord labels are educational aids, not a substitute for a teacher or a musician's judgment in every musical context.</p>
   <h2>Personal practice and content</h2>
   <p>You may use the interactive tools and save diagrams or printable references for your own learning and practice. The site’s original written explanations, illustrations and branding are not offered as an unrestricted commercial content library. The underlying software components may have separate licenses described in the <a href="/open-source/">open-source notices</a>.</p>
   <h2>Your performances and third-party services</h2>
   <p>Recordings you make in the browser are stored or downloaded locally as described in our <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>. The site does not claim ownership of your original performances. You are responsible for ensuring you have appropriate rights to any copyrighted music you record, publish, or upload elsewhere. When you choose to share a file with TikTok, X or another external service, that service’s own terms apply.</p>
   <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
   <p>We work to make chord formulas, diagrams and browser features reliable, but devices and audio/video formats vary, and mistakes or technical interruptions may occur. Check important note spellings and save your local work. The features and supported browsers may change as the project evolves.</p>
   <h2>Appropriate use and contact</h2>
   <ul>
    <li>Use the interactive tools lawfully and avoid interfering with the website or other visitors.</li>
    <li>Respect applicable copyright rules when sharing music or reproducing site materials.</li>
    <li>Report suspected music-theory errors, accessibility defects or technical issues so they can be corrected.</li>
   </ul>
   <p>Questions about site use can be sent to <a href="mailto:contact@pianochordexplorer.com">contact@pianochordexplorer.com</a>. See <a href="/about/">About and editorial methodology</a> for the project's source explanations and feedback channels.</p>
  </article>
 </section>
</BaseLayout>
